{
  "id": "sound_intensity__power_and_pressure_levels",
  "title": "Sound Intensity, Power and Pressure Levels",
  "description": "Calculate decibel levels for sound power, intensity, and pressure. Understand logarithmic ratios of physical values using reference standards for hearing threshold.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Measurement Type",
        "Signal/Value",
        "Reference Value",
        "Formula",
        "Level (dB)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Sound Power Level",
          "N (W)",
          "10⁻¹² W",
          "LN = 10 log(N / Nref)",
          "=10*LOG10(inputs.sound_power/1e-12)"
        ],
        [
          "Sound Intensity Level",
          "I (W/m²)",
          "10⁻¹² W/m²",
          "LI = 10 log(I / Iref)",
          "=10*LOG10(inputs.sound_intensity/1e-12)"
        ],
        [
          "Sound Pressure Level",
          "p (Pa)",
          "2×10⁻⁵ Pa",
          "Lp = 20 log(p / pref)",
          "=20*LOG10(inputs.sound_pressure/2e-5)"
        ],
        [
          "General Signal Level",
          "S (Signal Unit)",
          "Sref (Signal Unit)",
          "L = 10 log(S / Sref)",
          "=10*LOG10(inputs.signal/inputs.signal_ref)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "sound_power",
          "label": "Sound Power",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "W",
          "defaultValue": 0.000001
        },
        {
          "id": "sound_intensity",
          "label": "Sound Intensity",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "W/m²",
          "defaultValue": 0.000001
        },
        {
          "id": "sound_pressure",
          "label": "Sound Pressure",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "defaultValue": 0.02
        },
        {
          "id": "signal",
          "label": "Signal Value",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "signal_ref",
          "label": "Reference Signal Value",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "sound_power_level",
          "label": "Sound Power Level",
          "unit": "dB",
          "formula": "=10*LOG10(inputs.sound_power/1e-12)",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "sound_intensity_level",
          "label": "Sound Intensity Level",
          "unit": "dB",
          "formula": "=10*LOG10(inputs.sound_intensity/1e-12)",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "sound_pressure_level",
          "label": "Sound Pressure Level",
          "unit": "dB",
          "formula": "=20*LOG10(inputs.sound_pressure/2e-5)",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "general_signal_level",
          "label": "General Signal Level",
          "unit": "dB",
          "formula": "=10*LOG10(inputs.signal/inputs.signal_ref)",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Reference Standards\n\n**Sound Power Level (Lp):**\n- Reference: 10⁻¹² W (threshold of hearing)\n- Range: 0 dB (barely audible) to ~170 dB (jet aircraft)\n- Formula: Lp = 10 log(N / 10⁻¹²)\n\n**Sound Intensity Level (Li):**\n- Reference: 10⁻¹² W/m²\n- Formula: Li = 10 log(I / 10⁻¹²)\n\n**Sound Pressure Level (Lp):**\n- Reference: 2×10⁻⁵ Pa (threshold of hearing)\n- Formula: Lp = 20 log(p / 2×10⁻⁵)\n- Note: Doubling pressure increases level by 6 dB\n\n**General Decibel Formula:**\n- L = 10 log(S / Sref)"
    }
  ]
}